00:28:28.916 --> 00:28:31.210
these people did our people.

496
00:28:32.794 --> 00:28:34.880
When I was 10 years old...

497
00:28:36.006 --> 00:28:39.635
1970. his picture was

498
00:28:39.718 --> 00:28:41.720
all over the front page.

499
00:28:46.808 --> 00:28:48.352
He was everywhere.

500
00:28:51.438 --> 00:28:55.651
I think my mother knew
that my dad is Charles Manson.

501
00:28:56.902 --> 00:28:59.738
I remember my mother
cornered me in a bathroom...

502
00:29:03.075 --> 00:29:04.675
beat the hell outta me.

503
00:29:06.245 --> 00:29:09.373
The vacuum cleaner cord. the plug end...

504
00:29:10.999 --> 00:29:12.542
for about five minutes.

505
00:29:14.962 --> 00:29:16.380
I didn't do anything.

506
00:29:19.424 --> 00:29:23.428
It was just her venting her shame
and her rage out on me.

507
00:29:30.519 --> 00:29:32.938
I'm doing some research now.

508
00:29:33.522 --> 00:29:36.525
and the similarities
between my dad and Charles

509
00:29:36.608 --> 00:29:38.819
are kind of eerie from birth.

510
00:29:39.611 --> 00:29:42.406
Charles Manson was born
to a teenage mother

511
00:29:42.489 --> 00:29:44.783
and a father that disappeared.

512
00:29:44.866 --> 00:29:49.371
My dad was born in 1959 to a mother

513
00:29:49.454 --> 00:29:51.873
who was a teenager. was 17 years old.

514
00:29:51.957 --> 00:29:55.627
and a father who just disappeared.

515
00:29:55.711 --> 00:30:00.007
Charles Manson was my age
when he met my grandmother.

516
00:30:00.590 --> 00:30:02.926
and he went by the name of Charlie Dear.

517
00:30:03.635 --> 00:30:08.640
Um. he had just gotten
out of prison for pimping.

518
00:30:09.474 --> 00:30:12.561
The story goes that
they met at a bus stop.

519
00:30:12.644 --> 00:30:15.814
and they had a one-night.
possibly two-night stand.

520
00:30:16.857 --> 00:30:18.900
When my grandmother
realized she was pregnant.

521
00:30:18.984 --> 00:30:21.069
Charlie was back in prison.

522
00:30:21.153 --> 00:30:26.158
He was sentenced 10 years
for forging a $37.50 check.

523
00:30:26.241 --> 00:30:28.660
It's sad to think he could've
stayed with our family.

524
00:30:28.744 --> 00:30:30.954
but maybe he was more comfortable

525
00:30:31.038 --> 00:30:33.498
with the only family he had ever known.

526
00:30:33.999 --> 00:30:37.294
Manson. essentially.
he's in jail from the time he's 12

527
00:30:37.377 --> 00:30:39.880
'til he gets out in 1967.

528
00:30:39.963 --> 00:30:41.274
There's a larger cultural truth here.

529
00:30:41.298 --> 00:30:44.092
which is that. like.
incarceration breaks people.

530
00:30:46.970 --> 00:30:49.348
Manson's a gr...
like. a great example of that.

531
00:30:49.431 --> 00:30:51.433
of. like. being incarcerated
at a young age

532
00:30:51.516 --> 00:30:54.227
means you're gonna carry stuff out

533
00:30:54.311 --> 00:30:55.997
that's gonna make it
really impossible for you

534
00:30:56.021 --> 00:30:57.731
to be. like. normally functioning.

535
00:30:57.814 --> 00:30:59.608
And I think he would
say that in interviews.

536
00:30:59.691 --> 00:31:01.294
He would be like.
"I'm not from your world."

537
00:31:01.318 --> 00:31:03.087
-Right.
-"I was incarcerated my whole life.

538
00:31:03.111 --> 00:31:04.172
-I'm not from your world."
-That's right. Oh. yeah.

539
00:31:04.196 --> 00:31:06.236
Oh. he literally put it
in the language of "family."

540
00:31:06.323 --> 00:31:07.967
I've been in jail all my life.

541
00:31:07.991 --> 00:31:10.094
All the men in the joint raised me up.
told me what to do.

542
00:31:10.118 --> 00:31:11.161
what was right and wrong.

543
00:31:11.244 --> 00:31:12.388
Told me when to sit down. stand up.

544
00:31:12.412 --> 00:31:13.747
I just did everything I was told.

545
00:31:13.830 --> 00:31:15.332
-He performed a lot.
-Yeah.

546
00:31:15.415 --> 00:31:17.393
But when he said that.
I don't think he was performing.

547
00:31:17.417 --> 00:31:18.418
Yeah.

548
00:31:18.502 --> 00:31:21.380
How and when did he create
the Manson Family?

549
00:31:22.547 --> 00:31:25.926
So. Manson comes out of jail in 1967.

550
00:31:26.009 --> 00:31:27.886
hits San Francisco Summer of Love.

551
00:31:27.969 --> 00:31:31.306
This is the kind of. like.
coming out summer

552
00:31:31.390 --> 00:31:34.434
of the counterculture. of their practices.

553
00:31:34.518 --> 00:31:36.311
which include free love.

554
00:31:36.895 --> 00:31:38.688
Manson. he's got big eyes.

555
00:31:38.772 --> 00:31:41.108
He's not. like. standard hippie age.
he's in his 30s.

556
00:31:41.191 --> 00:31:42.991
And he starts meeting women
in the Bay Area...

557
00:31:43.735 --> 00:31:45.779
and kind of gathering his tribe.

558
00:31:50.117 --> 00:31:51.219
What were that women like?

559
00:31:51.243 --> 00:31:52.563
Did they come from good families?

560
00:31:52.619 --> 00:31:54.413
Did they have family of their own?

561
00:31:54.496 --> 00:31:57.749
If you read the press coverage
of the Manson women.

562
00:31:57.833 --> 00:32:00.001
they were almost. you know.

563
00:32:00.085 --> 00:32:03.171
unanimously depicted
as these. like. witches.

564
00:32:03.255 --> 00:32:06.758
these terrible. like. purposefully evil.

565
00:32:06.842 --> 00:32:09.428
hypersexualized druggies.

566
00:32:09.511 --> 00:32:11.221
But I really resist that.

567
00:32:11.304 --> 00:32:13.765
I'm. I'm really interested
in thinking about them

568
00:32:13.849 --> 00:32:15.267
as abused women.

569
00:32:15.809 --> 00:32:17.519
Mostly. they're runaways.

570
00:32:17.602 --> 00:32:19.521
Young women who found their way out.

571
00:32:19.604 --> 00:32:21.398
as so many young people did in that era.

572
00:32:21.481 --> 00:32:25.735
to California as a place
that seemed safer. freer.

573
00:32:26.736 --> 00:32:29.406
They moved down
to Southern California in '68.

574
00:32:29.489 --> 00:32:31.449
fairly well established
what we call the "Family."

575
00:32:31.700 --> 00:32:34.262
They call it "The Family."
they're brothers and sisters.

576
00:32:34.286 --> 00:32:35.966
They just lived anywhere
they felt like it.

577
00:32:36.121 --> 00:32:37.789
They were constantly taking dope

578
00:32:37.873 --> 00:32:40.333
and drinking wine and stealing cars.

579
00:32:59.186 --> 00:33:01.605
He's a good person. Very good person.

580
00:33:01.688 --> 00:33:03.064
Kinda had a peace.

581
00:33:03.565 --> 00:33:04.917
He named her "Squeaky"

582
00:33:04.941 --> 00:33:08.570
and she became one of the first members
of his so-called Family.

583
00:33:09.738 --> 00:33:11.507
There's an amazing documentary
that came out

584
00:33:11.531 --> 00:33:13.658
that had amazing footage from Spahn Ranch

585
00:33:13.742 --> 00:33:16.161
where. you know.
like. Lynette Fromme is. like. like.

586
00:33:16.244 --> 00:33:18.079
posed there with. like. a rifle. you know.

587
00:33:18.163 --> 00:33:21.041
And she really wants to vibe.

588
00:33:21.124 --> 00:33:25.462
like. scary. chaotic energy.

589
00:33:25.545 --> 00:33:27.825
Though not involved
in the Tate-LaBianca murders.

590
00:33:27.881 --> 00:33:29.799
she served over 30 years

591
00:33:29.883 --> 00:33:32.093
for attempting
to assassinate President Ford

592
00:33:32.177 --> 00:33:34.471
to protest environmental destruction.

593
00:33:34.554 --> 00:33:36.848
Can I ask if I can record this?

594
00:33:37.849 --> 00:33:39.849
-Yes.
-Okay. thank you.

595
00:33:40.185 --> 00:33:43.313
I. I wanna start from the. the beginning.

596
00:33:44.272 --> 00:33:46.858
With Charlie. we were a very...

597
00:33:47.567 --> 00:33:51.696
cohesive female energy.

598
00:33:51.780 --> 00:33:54.199
We were going day to day.

599
00:33:54.282 --> 00:33:59.037
and we were opening ourselves up

600
00:33:59.120 --> 00:34:04.751
to that experience
of pretty much the universe.

601
00:34:06.878 --> 00:34:09.714
Most of us wanted to be with Charlie.

602
00:34:09.798 --> 00:34:12.842
I don't think there was
any doubt about that.

603
00:34:12.926 --> 00:34:17.138
He thought the more
people became part of it.

604
00:34:17.931 --> 00:34:19.641
the better it would be.

605
00:34:22.060 --> 00:34:23.420
I know other Manson girls

606
00:34:23.478 --> 00:34:26.189
have much darker memories
of my grandfather.

607
00:34:26.731 --> 00:34:29.943
I contacted Dianne Lake.
also known as "Snake."

608
00:34:30.026 --> 00:34:32.445
who was 14 when she joined the Family.

609
00:34:34.114 --> 00:34:35.800
Are you in a space where you feel okay

610
00:34:35.824 --> 00:34:36.908
about tomorrow?

611
00:34:38.702 --> 00:34:40.412
-Yeah.
-Yeah?

612
00:34:40.495 --> 00:34:43.456
Yeah. it's always
gonna be a little tough. Um...

613
00:34:44.749 --> 00:34:46.835
It's the first time meeting a victim.

614
00:34:47.419 --> 00:34:52.132
I wish for you. you don't have
to wear this so heavy on your shoulders.

615
00:34:52.215 --> 00:34:56.636
Like. you take on so many people's
struggles to try to understand them.

616
00:34:58.096 --> 00:35:00.098
Well. listen. hang in there. okay?

617
00:35:00.181 --> 00:35:02.559
-Okay. thank you.
-Alright. thank you.

618
00:35:02.642 --> 00:35:04.162
-Talk soon. Bye.
-Bye.

619
00:35:05.854 --> 00:35:08.565
How did you meet my grandfather?

620
00:35:08.648 --> 00:35:12.527
I had a really big disconnect
with my parents.

621
00:35:12.611 --> 00:35:15.113
And then. I had this. um...

622
00:35:15.614 --> 00:35:20.327
this acid trip where I. I heard God
tell me it was time for me to leave home.

623
00:35:21.453 --> 00:35:23.455
I hitchhiked to LA

624
00:35:23.538 --> 00:35:28.376
and shortly after I got there.
I go to this party.

625
00:35:28.460 --> 00:35:30.879
Lynette comes out...

626
00:35:31.671 --> 00:35:34.883
"Dianne! Charlie!
Dianne is here!" You know?

627
00:35:34.966 --> 00:35:36.885
And gives me a big embrace.

628
00:35:36.968 --> 00:35:40.347
And Charlie gets up
from the. you know. the circle.

629
00:35:40.430 --> 00:35:43.016
offers me. you know.
a sip of his root beer

630
00:35:43.433 --> 00:35:46.603
and was totally enamored
with him. you know?

631
00:35:46.686 --> 00:35:49.105
I mean. here I was loved. embraced.

632
00:35:49.189 --> 00:35:51.024
Charlie took me to the bus that night

633
00:35:51.107 --> 00:35:54.027
and made love to me
like I had never experienced

634
00:35:54.110 --> 00:35:55.403
before in my life.

635
00:35:56.029 --> 00:35:58.823
I felt truly loved as a woman. you know.

636
00:35:58.907 --> 00:36:02.035
and not just a kid
being taken advantage of.

637
00:36:02.118 --> 00:36:04.704
So. um. I hopped on the bus.

638
00:36:04.788 --> 00:36:07.791
That's when we got
connected to Spahn Ranch.

639
00:36:08.875 --> 00:36:11.169
-Charlie would play the guitar...
-Mm-hmm.

640
00:36:11.252 --> 00:36:13.612
and we would. you know. sing along.

641
00:36:14.047 --> 00:36:17.634
Charlie had this way of combining music.

642
00:36:17.717 --> 00:36:20.845
things from the Bible.
things from Buddhism.

643
00:36:20.929 --> 00:36:24.307
He had this ability
to weave all that together.

644
00:36:24.391 --> 00:36:27.727
so that it sounded really.
ooh. special and...

645
00:36:27.811 --> 00:36:31.564
Like. he had a special inside gift.

646
00:36:32.732 --> 00:36:35.485
That was kind of his hold on us.

647
00:36:36.778 --> 00:36:38.988
I think he got a Messiah complex.

648
00:36:41.991 --> 00:36:44.387
Manson is generally.
and his Family. are generally understood

649
00:36:44.411 --> 00:36:46.746
as part of the counterculture.
but they're really like.

650
00:36:46.830 --> 00:36:50.500
they've taken a ladle and just kind of.
like. scooped the top. you know. surface.

651
00:36:50.583 --> 00:36:53.211
He gets the free love part. for sure.

652
00:36:53.878 --> 00:36:56.131
He gets the drug part. for sure.

653
00:36:56.214 --> 00:36:57.507
But. like. this was a commune

654
00:36:57.590 --> 00:37:00.093
that was organized
for the benefit of one man.

655
00:37:00.969 --> 00:37:03.680
He was a con man. you know.
He was a manipulator.

656
00:37:03.763 --> 00:37:06.516
He was approaching them not with empathy

657
00:37:06.599 --> 00:37:08.435
or with. you know. solidarity.

658
00:37:08.518 --> 00:37:11.980
but with this notion that he could
get from them what he wanted.

659
00:37:12.063 --> 00:37:16.109
So. they steal. they sell drugs.
they also creepy crawl.

660
00:37:16.192 --> 00:37:19.863
And that's the one crime that. um.
I think folks don't talk about enough.

661
00:37:20.613 --> 00:37:22.115
Manson and some of the girls.

662
00:37:22.198 --> 00:37:25.493
and whoever was around up at night

663
00:37:25.577 --> 00:37:29.539
would go out in a crew.
in a couple cars. and just pick a house

664
00:37:29.622 --> 00:37:32.000
where the people were sleeping.

665
00:37:32.542 --> 00:37:35.628
They would break into houses
in... around the LA area.

666
00:37:35.712 --> 00:37:40.383
and they'd literally go in
and rearrange the furniture and leave.

667
00:37:40.467 --> 00:37:42.010
Like. they would change enough.

668
00:37:42.093 --> 00:37:44.012
so that the folks
would wake up and know.

669
00:37:44.095 --> 00:37:45.221
"We've been invaded."

670
00:37:45.764 --> 00:37:49.517
When he
started taking the girls on creepy crawls.

671
00:37:49.601 --> 00:37:51.041
he was actually getting 'em used to.

672
00:37:51.102 --> 00:37:54.147
you know. burglaries
and calling it something cute.

673
00:37:54.230 --> 00:37:56.733
As part of his
patriarchal control of the Family.

674
00:37:57.358 --> 00:37:59.819
Manson. uh. is a trip master.

675
00:38:01.529 --> 00:38:04.449
I mean. it was very much tied up
with his sexual control of the family.

676
00:38:04.532 --> 00:38:06.576
Like. he would get people tripping wildly.

677
00:38:06.659 --> 00:38:10.163
and then arrange.
you know. various couplings.

678
00:38:10.246 --> 00:38:12.248
When I was with Charlie. we took...

679
00:38:12.332 --> 00:38:17.128
anywhere between 30 and 40 trips
on-on acid alone.

680
00:38:17.212 --> 00:38:19.506
That's not counting
all psilocybin and mescaline

681
00:38:19.589 --> 00:38:21.132
and little opium.

682
00:38:21.216 --> 00:38:24.177
They went through
their acid trips together.

683
00:38:24.260 --> 00:38:27.222
They went through their
group sex things together.

684
00:38:27.305 --> 00:38:29.224
But it was always Charlie's will.

685
00:38:29.307 --> 00:38:32.185
Everyone was subservient
to Charlie's will no matter what.

686
00:38:32.268 --> 00:38:33.603
He was the father.

687
00:38:34.604 --> 00:38:37.816
Manson is trying
to. uh. advance his music career

688
00:38:37.899 --> 00:38:41.653
through the vehicle of his...
the women of his family

689
00:38:41.736 --> 00:38:44.364
by making them. you know. available.

690
00:38:44.447 --> 00:38:47.325
um. to a wide range of music industry men.

691
00:38:47.408 --> 00:38:49.244
Was he pimping you guys at the time?

692
00:38:49.327 --> 00:38:51.663
-Kind of. For favors.
-Hmm.

693
00:38:51.746 --> 00:38:53.832
You know. it wasn't
outright. like. for money.

694
00:38:53.915 --> 00:38:57.126
but it was definitely for favors.

695
00:38:58.169 --> 00:39:02.298
Charlie invited myself
and another. uh. young lady. Gale.

696
00:39:02.382 --> 00:39:05.009
to go swimming at Dennis Wilson's house.

697
00:39:05.093 --> 00:39:06.511
Come on! The Beach Boys?!

698
00:39:06.594 --> 00:39:08.197
They were. you know.
they were. like. on a par

699
00:39:08.221 --> 00:39:09.806
with The Beatles at that point.

700
00:39:09.889 --> 00:39:12.517
These are. like. central guys
in the music industry.

701
00:39:13.059 --> 00:39:15.728
Terry Melcher's a major producer.

702
00:39:15.812 --> 00:39:17.122
They were going out to Spahn Ranch

703
00:39:17.146 --> 00:39:20.275
and having sex with yo...
really young women

704
00:39:20.358 --> 00:39:23.403
because they knew that Charlie
would sort of. like. curate that for them.

705
00:39:23.486 --> 00:39:24.922
I didn't come to Terry Melcher.

706
00:39:24.946 --> 00:39:28.616
He come to me with money in his hand.
He offered me. I didn't ask him.

707
00:39:28.700 --> 00:39:30.451
He had kind of puffed himself up

708
00:39:30.535 --> 00:39:32.203
with this new idea about himself.

709
00:39:32.287 --> 00:39:33.454
He was Daddy of this family.

710
00:39:33.538 --> 00:39:35.206
He was gonna be a famous rock star.

711
00:39:35.290 --> 00:39:37.041
and there were plenty of people around him

712
00:39:37.125 --> 00:39:38.877
who thought he was really talented.

713
00:39:38.960 --> 00:39:40.920
Neil Young is one of the few people

714
00:39:41.004 --> 00:39:44.257
who's been willing to go on record
saying that Manson had a lot of talent.

715
00:39:44.340 --> 00:39:47.552
And so. when he went
for his official music audition

716
00:39:47.635 --> 00:39:49.846
with Terry Melcher in a studio.

717
00:39:49.929 --> 00:39:52.932
Manson thinks he's gonna
get a. a record contract.

718
00:39:53.016 --> 00:39:54.517
And then he doesn't.

719
00:39:54.601 --> 00:39:57.228
And I think that really
sends Manson around the bend.

720
00:39:57.896 --> 00:40:01.399
When I went into
Dennis Wilson's. uh. Beach Boys.

721
00:40:01.482 --> 00:40:03.985
I said. "You owe me money for music.
Where's the money?"

722
00:40:04.068 --> 00:40:07.030
They put me
onto the Italian business manager.

723
00:40:07.488 --> 00:40:10.533
He... I said. "Don't I get something
for this music here?"

724
00:40:10.617 --> 00:40:13.286
And he said. "No. you get nothing."

725
00:40:13.369 --> 00:40:14.787
He said. "Sue me."

726
00:40:14.871 --> 00:40:17.040
I said. "I won't sue you.
I'll bomb your car. man.

727
00:40:17.123 --> 00:40:18.458
I'll blow your house up."

728
00:40:22.670 --> 00:40:24.339
I'm speaking to Ed Roach.

729
00:40:24.797 --> 00:40:25.957
We were texting this morning.

730
00:40:26.007 --> 00:40:27.800
He was the Beach Boys photographer.

731
00:40:27.884 --> 00:40:29.904
Really good friends with Dennis Wilson.

732
00:40:31.304 --> 00:40:34.140
My dad and I. we loved The Beach Boys.

733
00:40:35.099 --> 00:40:36.643
So. this is kind of crazy.

734
00:40:39.062 --> 00:40:40.647
Kind of excited.

735
00:40:42.273 --> 00:40:43.792
-This is you? Wow.
-Yeah. that's me.

736
00:40:43.816 --> 00:40:48.446
That's. uh. 1971 or '73 maybe. uh.

737
00:40:48.529 --> 00:40:50.323
shooting The Beach Boys with Dennis.

738
00:40:50.406 --> 00:40:51.842
These photos that you're picking up.

739
00:40:51.866 --> 00:40:54.160
this was. uh. the very first time.

740
00:40:54.243 --> 00:40:57.205
the only time that I ever
went up to Spahn Ranch. uh.

